Invent Yourself scripsit:

> If "mi speni lo ninmu" is the best you can say, then you couldn't pick
> your wife out of a lineup.

If that's *all* he can say, then yes.

> Similarly, asking with "mi nitcu lo mikce" is
> perfectly valid, because without further specification any doctor is
> acceptable. 

Not at all. Without further specification, there is *some* doctor that
is acceptable, but there is no saying which one it is. If you say
"mi nitcu lo mikce", then the only way to falsify this is if you
reject *every* doctor as not the one you need.

